{"task_id": "HumanEval/60", "solution": "def sum_to_n(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the sum of integers from 1 to n (inclusive).\n\n    Examples:\n    >>> sum_to_n(30)\n    465\n    >>> sum_to_n(100)\n    5050\n    >>> sum_to_n(5)\n    15\n    >>> sum_to_n(10)\n    55\n    >>> sum_to_n(1)\n    1\n\n    Behavior:\n    - n must be an integer (TypeError raised otherwise).\n    - For n < 1 the function returns 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n < 1:\n        return 0\n    return n * (n + 1) // 2"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "def largest_prime_factor(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n.\n    Handles even factors then odd trial division.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_prime_factor = 1\n\n    # Handle factors of 2.\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        max_prime_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors starting from 3.\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            max_prime_factor = i\n            n //= i\n        i += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be the largest prime factor.\n    if n > 1:\n        max_prime_factor = n\n\n    return max_prime_factor"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "def derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs represent coefficients of a polynomial.\n    xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[2] * x^2 + ....\n     Return derivative of this polynomial in the same form.\n    >>> derivative([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    [1, 4, 12, 20]\n    >>> derivative([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 6]\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(xs)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return []\n    result = []\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        result.append(i * xs[i])\n    return result"}
