{"task_id": "HumanEval/119", "solution": "def match_parens(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if two parenthesis strings can be concatenated in some order to form a balanced string.\n    Returns 'Yes' if possible, otherwise 'No'.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_good(s):\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a string 's' is a balanced parentheses string.\n        Returns True if balanced, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        balance = 0\n        for ch in s:\n            if ch == '(':\n                balance += 1\n            else:  # ch == ')'\n                balance -= 1\n            if balance < 0:\n                return False\n        return balance == 0\n\n    s1 = lst[0]\n    s2 = lst[1]\n\n    if is_good(s1 + s2) or is_good(s2 + s1):\n        return 'Yes'\n    else:\n        return 'No'"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/120", "solution": "import heapq\ndef maximum(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a list arr of integers and an integer k, return a new list of length k\n    containing the k largest numbers from arr, sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_k = heapq.nlargest(k, arr)\n    return sorted(largest_k)"}
